story += [P('7. PLAGIARISM REPORT','Chap'),P('No similarity score or certificate is included or claimed here. BIT Mesra’s June 2021 policy requires project reports to undergo a plagiarism check, requires a copy of the report to accompany submission, sets an allowable limit of confidence of 10% after stated exclusions, and makes the supervisor responsible for the check. Confirm the applicable exclusions and submission route with the guide before relying on a percentage.','BodyX'),P('The BIT Central Library publishes an iThenticate similarity-check service. Its current service page says users may send a PDF or DOCX to library@bitmesra.ac.in with their name, registration number and course/branch; it also notes direct submission to the library with a report returned to the registered BIT email. The page specifically limits account creation to faculty, research scholars and postgraduate students, so undergraduate students should contact the guide and library first to confirm that direct report generation is available for this B.Tech report. This institutional route is the best no-cost route to ask about; the published page does not state a fee. The supervisor is responsible for the formal check under the Institute policy.','BodyX'),P('Do not treat a public free checker as an official BIT certificate. Its database coverage may differ, and uploading unpublished work may raise privacy concerns. Review any matches, cite sources, and quote borrowed text correctly; no tool can guarantee a particular score.','BodyX'),P('ATTACH OFFICIAL SIMILARITY / PLAGIARISM REPORT HERE AFTER INSTITUTE CHECK','Sec'),P('[Reserved attachment page. Insert the original report generated through the Institute-approved process; no score, certificate, or checker identity is fabricated in this draft.]','Ctr')]
